// Each of a child's three streams goes, in turn, to each Stdio: this program's own
// (inherit), the null device (ignore), a file, and a pipe. The child copies its input
// into its output, and writes ERR to its error.
// The child is tests/helpers/child.ctx, as `echo`: it writes `OUT[` its input `]`. The program
// is given `from parent` as its own input, the file in holds `from file`, and the program
// writes `piped input` into a pipe. What went to a pipe the program prints after `out pipe: `
// or `err pipe: `; what went to its own streams is in its output as it is.
//# build child: {home}/tests/helpers/child.ctx
//# build program: main.ctx

// stdin inherit, stdout ignore, stderr file
//# write in0 escaped:
//| from file\
//# $ {program} {child} inherit ignore file in0 out0 err0
//# stdin escaped:
//| from parent\
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| exit 0
//# file out0 escaped:
//| \
//# file err0 escaped:
//| ERR\

// stdin ignore, stdout file, stderr pipe
//# write in1 escaped:
//| from file\
//# $ {program} {child} ignore file pipe in1 out1 err1
//# stdin escaped:
//| from parent\
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| err pipe: ERR
//| exit 0
//# file out1 escaped:
//| OUT[]\
//# file err1 escaped:
//| \

// stdin file, stdout pipe, stderr inherit
//# write in2 escaped:
//| from file\
//# $ {program} {child} file pipe inherit in2 out2 err2
//# stdin escaped:
//| from parent\
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| out pipe: OUT[from file]
//| exit 0
//# stderr escaped:
//| ERR\
//# file out2 escaped:
//| \
//# file err2 escaped:
//| \

// stdin pipe, stdout inherit, stderr ignore
//# write in3 escaped:
//| from file\
//# $ {program} {child} pipe inherit ignore in3 out3 err3
//# stdin escaped:
//| from parent\
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| OUT[piped input]exit 0
//# file out3 escaped:
//| \
//# file err3 escaped:
//| \
